1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,234
Most AI history tools sound sure of themselves, and you cannot tell what is real. So I built a radio station that is not allowed to guess.

2
00:00:09,784 --> 00:00:21,630
This is Ghost Town Radio. It began with Bodie, California. Now it also tunes Bangalore, Coorg, Hyderabad and Mumbai, from public domain newspapers, gazetteers and books.

3
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:28,816
Pick a town with these buttons. Each town has its own sources, its own schedule, and its own silent hours.

4
00:00:29,366 --> 00:00:33,421
Turn the dial to pick an hour. It works by touch, mouse, or keyboard.

5
00:00:33,971 --> 00:00:41,050
Press play. The D J is fictional. But look at the card. Every line shows the exact quote, and a link to the page.

6
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:54,068
DJ Hollis Vane (fictional): The chapel of Mount Carmel was erected in the year 1721.

7
00:00:54,518 --> 00:00:59,824
Quote: “The chapel of Mount Carmel, was erected in 1721.”

8
00:01:00,024 --> 00:01:06,117
The quote is word for word, typos and all. A code check rejects any quote that is not in the source.

9
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:11,188
Some hours are silent. When the archive has nothing, the D J says nothing.

10
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:23,714
Across the five towns, one hundred twenty claims are on air, and every quote passes the code check. I read the new ones by hand, and threw out eighteen of one hundred fourteen that did not hold up.

11
00:01:24,264 --> 00:01:27,916
It is open source, and the link is below. Ghost Town Radio.

